    <string name="picks_history">History buff picks: the Gateway of India and its harbour ferries, the UNESCO-listed CSMT terminus, the Vastu Sangrahalaya museum, and the rock-cut Elephanta Caves make a classic heritage trail.</string>
    <string name="picks_foodie">Foodie picks: browse Colaba Causeway, stop at Leopold Cafe, have bun maska at Kyani &amp; Co., then try street snacks at Girgaon Chowpatty and Juhu Beach. Check opening hours locally.</string>
    <string name="picks_nature">Nature picks: sunrise along Marine Drive, greenery at Hanging Gardens, deer and trails at Sanjay Gandhi National Park, and the sea vistas of the Bandra-Worli Sea Link.</string>
    <string name="picks_photo">Photography picks: golden hour at the Gateway of India, the Queen’s Necklace curve of Marine Drive, the sweeping Bandra-Worli Sea Link, and dusk crowds at Girgaon Chowpatty.</string>
    <string name="more_city_title">Offline city guide</string>
    <string name="more_city_body">Fort and Colaba hold much of Mumbai’s heritage architecture. Marine Drive and the Worli Sea Link are best around sunset. Juhu Beach fills up for street food in the evening. Joggers use Marine Drive early morning and Shivaji Park afternoons.</string>
